      "text": "Access Control. Lost: $66K"
    },
    {
      "source": "RevertIQ",
      "text": "On 2024-11-20, the MainnetSettler contract on Ethereum was used to execute an arbitrary ERC20 transferFrom against a wallet that had previously approved the contract to spend HOLD tokens. The attacker drained about 308.45 million HOLD tokens, valued at roughly $66,000 at the time of the incident. A wallet had granted the MainnetSettler contract a large HOLD token allowance, and the contract's execution flow allowed externally supplied call data to trigger arbitrary token operations. The attacker used this capability to execute a transferFrom against the approved wallet and move HOLD tokens to an attacker-controlled address."
    }
  ],
